<link rel="stylesheet" href="css/site-layout.css?v=20261010-layout2"></head><body><?php require __DIR__ . '/includes/site-header.php'; ?><main class="shell legal-page"><section class="intro"><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>How BNB RWA Hub handles conversation, wallet, transaction and technical information.</p><div class="legal-effective">Effective date: October 8, 2026</div></section>
<section class="legal-card"><h2>1. Overview</h2><p>This Privacy Policy explains how BNB RWA Hub processes information when you use the dashboard, Ask Hubble, wallet connection, quote, purchase and sale features. BNB RWA Hub is designed as an experimental hackathon project and does not require a user account.</p></section>
<section class="legal-card"><h2>2. Information we process</h2><ul><li><strong>Conversation data:</strong> prompts, conversation responses, conversation state and request identifiers needed to restore and continue your Hubble session.</li><li><strong>Wallet and transaction data:</strong> public wallet addresses, selected token/amount, transaction hashes, receipts, balances, allowances and other public blockchain information when you use wallet or trading features.</li><li><strong>Technical data:</strong> request timing, API response metadata, error information and limited server logs used to operate, secure and diagnose the service.</li><li><strong>Browser state:</strong> an essential first-party session cookie and browser storage used for conversation continuity, UI state and recovery of submitted or uncertain transactions.</li></ul><p>BNB RWA Hub does not ask for or intentionally collect your wallet seed phrase or private key. Wallet signatures and transaction approvals are handled by your wallet provider.</p></section>
<section class="legal-card"><h2>3. How information is used</h2><p>Information is used to provide the requested research or trading workflow, restore your conversation, prepare quotes, verify transaction status, prevent duplicate transaction requests, enforce product limits, diagnose failures and protect the service from abuse.</p></section>
<section class="legal-card"><h2>4. AI processing</h2><p>When you use Ask Hubble, your prompt and a limited amount of relevant recent conversation or RWA data may be sent to the AI model provider configured by the service so that Hubble can generate a response. Model providers are third-party services and may process requests under their own terms and privacy practices.</p><p>Do not submit secrets, seed phrases, private keys, passwords or other information that is not necessary for your request.</p></section>
<section class="legal-card"><h2>5. Binance, RPC and blockchain processing</h2><p>Market, RWA, quote and transaction preparation requests may use Binance Web3 APIs or other configured infrastructure. When a trading path requires a wallet address, public wallet and trade parameters may be included in those requests. Blockchain transactions and wallet addresses are public by design once broadcast and cannot be made private by this website.</p></section>
<section class="legal-card"><h2>6. Retention and deletion</h2><p>The conversation session is designed to remain available for seven days after your most recent activity while the essential session cookie remains available. Expired sessions may be removed by server cleanup.</p><p><strong>Clear conversation</strong> deletes the current saved conversation session and its associated messages from the application database and starts a fresh session. It does not erase information already transmitted to third-party providers, operational logs that may be retained for security or diagnostics, or public blockchain records.</p><p>Browser-side transaction recovery information may remain until the related transaction is resolved, the site clears it, or you clear site storage yourself. Clearing browser storage does not cancel a blockchain transaction that has already been submitted.</p></section>
<section class="legal-card"><h2>7. Cookies and local storage</h2><p>The site currently uses essential first-party browser storage for core functionality rather than advertising or behavioural tracking. See the <a href="cookies.php">Cookie Policy</a> for details.</p></section>
<section class="legal-card"><h2>8. Security and user responsibility</h2><p>Reasonable technical controls are used to reduce accidental disclosure and unauthorized access, but no website, API, wallet, model provider or blockchain system can be guaranteed completely secure. Protect your device, wallet and browser profile and independently verify wallet prompts before signing.</p></section>
<section class="legal-card"><h2>9. Your choices</h2><p>You can clear the current conversation, disconnect your wallet from the interface, clear this site's cookies/local storage in your browser and choose not to use Hubble or trading features. Public blockchain records are not controlled by BNB RWA Hub and cannot generally be deleted.</p></section>
<section class="legal-card"><h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2><p>This policy may be updated as the project, data sources, model providers or wallet features change. The effective date above will be updated when material changes are published.</p></section>
